# Stage 2 — Project Planning

## 1. Project Overview

The project is a web platform designed to help students find other students to work with on projects.

The main idea is to connect students who have different but complementary skills. For example, a student who knows how to code could find another student who is good at design, video editing, communication, or project management.

The goal is to make it easier for students to create projects together, find suitable teammates, and develop their skills through collaboration.

The project will be developed progressively, starting with the project idea and planning, followed by technical documentation and MVP development.

---

## 2. High-Level Plan

The project is divided into five main stages.

### Stage 1 — Idea Development

**Status:** Completed

During this stage, the project idea was defined and the main problem to solve was identified.

The project concept, target users, and main objectives were established.

**Main deliverables:**

* Project idea
* Problem identification
* Target users
* Project objectives
* Initial project scope

---

### Stage 2 — Project Planning

**Status:** In progress

This stage focuses on defining how the project will be developed and organizing the different phases of the project.

The main development stages, milestones, and expected deliverables are defined.

**Main deliverables:**

* High-level project plan
* Project timeline
* Project milestones
* Definition of the main project phases

---

### Stage 3 — Technical Documentation

**Status:** Planned

During this stage, the technical structure of the project will be defined before development begins.

The technologies, architecture, database structure, APIs, and main technical components will be documented.

**Main deliverables:**

* Technical architecture
* Database design
* API structure
* Technology choices
* Technical documentation

---

### Stage 4 — MVP Development

**Status:** Planned

During this stage, the first functional version of the platform will be developed.

The MVP will focus on the most important features needed to demonstrate the main idea of the project.

**Main deliverables:**

* User interface
* User authentication
* Student profiles
* Project creation
* Project discovery
* Student/project matching
* Basic collaboration features
* Functional MVP

---

### Stage 5 — Project Closure

**Status:** Planned

The final stage will focus on testing, fixing remaining problems, documenting the project, and preparing the final presentation.

The completed MVP will be reviewed to identify possible improvements and future features.

**Main deliverables:**

* Final testing
* Bug fixes
* Final documentation
* Project presentation
* Project review
* Future improvements

